      "message": "Thanks for splitting this out. It looks right to me: under x86_64 page size emulation the metadata area is `__PAGE_SIZE`, i.e. four kernel pages (see `perf_mmap_alloc_metadata_page()`), and `perf_mmap_rb()` has charged all four since `9bb7e0640feb` (`\"ANDROID: 16K: Fixup perf_mmap check for metadata page\"`). So `perf_mmap_close()` left three pages in `locked_vm` for every ring buffer. On arm64, `__PAGE_SIZE / PAGE_SIZE` is 1, so nothing changes there or for P3S.\n\nSince this fixes an emulation patch rather than P3S, would `ANDROID: 16K: perf: Balance emulated metadata page accounting` work as the subject, like the other emulation fixes (e.g. \"ANDROID: 16K: proc: Fix resident page count in task_statm\"), with `Fixes: 9bb7e0640feb`? It doesn\u0027t depend on the P3S series either, so it could go to android17-6.18 on its own, together with the AUX bound I mentioned on aosp/4367963.",
